From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:53:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 084/115] Register variables in procedures with
 try..except/try..finally where it is safe

A procedure with an explicit exception frame got no register variables at
all. optexcregvar.mark_exceptsafe_regvars, run before the locals and
parameters get their locations, marks the ones that may stay register
variables: those that no protected block writes and then needs afterwards
(in a handler, a finally block, outside the try statement, or implicitly as
the result or self), and, for a try statement inside a loop, that the block
writes before it reads. setjmp/longjmp restore the callee-saved registers, so
a value no protected block changed is intact in the handler; a value only
used inside the block is dead when the block is left by an exception.
tests/test/texcregvar1.pp covers the cases that must stay in memory.
